    "created_at": "2025-10-10T00:08:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-10T00:58:43Z",
    "body": "To clarify point 2 above, we may want to add a specific point that an element with a [custom element state](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-custom-element-state) that is *not* `undefined` or `uncustomized` should never mutate its `customElementRegistry`.\n\nDoing so would result in an element potentially having a different `customElementRegistry` from the one including the definition that upgraded it. That seems very confusing and hard to reason about.\n\nThe current behavior for this case is inconsistent between Canary and Safari. Safari mutates the customized element's registry. See [this example](https://codepen.io/Steve-Orvell/pen/jEWwqdg?editors=1000)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
